      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sibley was renamed in 1880 after Hiram Sibley, aligning the village name with the railroad station and post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sibley%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s post office began as Burr Oaks in 1873 before adopting the Sibley name a year later.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sibley%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1850s, Ohio‑born Sullivant bought vast prairie lands for intensive corn and cattle, employing hundreds and pioneering mechanized farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sibley_illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Facing the Panic of 1873, Sullivant sold the core property to Hiram Sibley in 1878, who reorganized it into a tenant‑farm system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sibley_illinois"
    },
    {
